{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795094380,"nonce":"wKG70iCRxzO+yLkApKxEQFIOj/I=","title":"Run page: a dropped log stream reconnects every 2s and replays the whole log","message":"Found in the run page review (2026-11-19). The run page reopens a step's log stream when it ends while the try is still running (proxy idle timeout, server roll). It reopens on a fixed 2s timer with no backoff, and each reopen replays the log from the start because the log SSE endpoint has no resume offset. A try behind a proxy that cuts idle connections, or an endpoint returning errors, reconnects every 2s for the life of the try.\n\nFix: backoff on repeated failures, and a resume offset (Last-Event-ID or ?from=\u003cbyte offset\u003e) on the log stream so a reopen fetches only new output. ui/scarab-web-ui/src/components/StepPane.tsx, src/api/client.ts streamStepLogs, server log SSE route.","files":null}]}